<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="41c7d249-0858-556c-9f14-33ec8535e82a" activityNameId="7c0c2178-bcd2-5b24-abef-f0104e6000be" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Barley grains organic, at farm</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Barley grains organic, at farm
Inventory refers to the production of 1 kg barley grains organic, at farm respectively barley straw organic, at farm , both with a moisture content of 15%. The multioutput-process barley organic delivers the co-products barley grains organic, at farm (4153kg yield/ha) and barley straw organic, at farm (2924kg yield/ha). Economic allocation with allocation factor of 91.3% to grains (exceptions see report).;
UUID: 88e07c72-0ef8-3a7b-a2c8-0bb1d162eb07
The inventory includes the processes of soil cultivation, sowing, weed control, fertilisation, harvest and grain drying. Machine infrastructure and a shed for machine sheltering is included. Inputs of fertilisers and seed as well as grain transports to the regional processing center (10km) are considered. The direct emissions on the field are also included.
Location: Refers to an average production in the Swiss lowlands.
Technology: Organic production
Time period: The yield data have been collected for the years 1996-2003.
Production volume: CH prod of barley: 257400t in 2004. % repr ref to fract of tot area in lowlands
Sampling: Data were compiled from statistics, pilot network, fertilising recommendations, documents from extension services, information provided by retailers and expert knowledge. The production data were verified and adjusted by a group of experts. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_88e07c72-0ef8-3a7b-a2c8-0bb1d162eb07.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
